course: dictionary
lesson: 8157
title: Who is a researcher?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A researcher is a person whose job is to study something carefully to find out new facts. When you meet this word, look at the words around it. «When researchers sprayed a harmless mist into single canopy trees, beetles of hundreds of kinds fell out.» Sprayed, trees and beetles tell you that researchers test things and watch what happens.
explain: Context can also show you the researcher's job. «It was reported that AI helped researchers spot faint ink in scans of the scrolls, so words could be read again.» The clues are faint ink, scans and words could be read again. A researcher looks closely, finds something new, and tells others about it.
explain: Some researchers work in a team. «A team of researchers» means several people working together on the same question. Phrases like «researchers found that» tell you what they discovered, and that is the most important part to remember.
explain: To check your meaning, swap a simple idea into the sentence. Try putting "scientist or careful studier" in place of researchers. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right. If it does not, read the words around it again.
fact: A researcher is a person who studies something carefully to discover new facts.
fact: Researchers can be scientists doing experiments, or people studying history or people.
fact: Researchers test their ideas, watch what happens, and check their results.
fact: «Researchers found that» is a useful phrase, because it tells you what was discovered.
fact: A «medical researcher» studies illness and health to help people get better.
exercise: «When researchers sprayed a harmless mist into single canopy trees, beetles of hundreds of kinds fell out.» What are the researchers doing in this sentence? | Cutting down the trees for wood | *Testing an idea to find out new facts | Hunting for a lost mist | Painting pictures of beetles
exercise: Nadia says a researcher is a teacher at school. What does researcher really mean? | A person who sells books in a shop | A person who teaches children at school | *A person who studies something carefully to find new facts | A person who drives a bus to town
exercise: «The researchers found that the scrolls were older than anyone thought.» What did the researchers find? | That the scrolls were lost forever | That the scrolls were made of gold | That the researchers were very tired | *That the scrolls were older than anyone thought
test: «A team of researchers tested the idea many times.» Why would a team test an idea many times? | *To check that the results are true | To make the test shorter | To avoid doing any real work | To win a prize for being fast
test: Which person is a researcher? | A shopkeeper who sells bread | A waiter who brings the food | *A scientist doing experiments to learn how plants grow | A driver who takes people to work
exam: «Medical researchers published their results so other people could check them.» Why do researchers publish their results? | *So others can check and learn from them | To stop anyone else from testing the idea | Hide them in a drawer | To make the results disappear
